# The call of a named body with no source of its free name fails at a call
# (docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#dynamic): make calls y, whose z nothing binds -- not
# a caller, not an inherited input, not y's lexical space. make only hands z on,
# and the root's call of make, where the chain starts, has no source of it: that
# call is refused, as any required input that no one can give, and not the
# definition of y.
fn: make () int
    y: z + 1
    y()
    return: 7
end: make

int: got make()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: got; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
